<title>MEXICO: Banco de Mexico completes secondary intervention.</title>
<headline>Banco de Mexico completes secondary intervention.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-06-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Banco de Mexico placed all three direct sales of paper and nine repurchase agreements whereby it had sought to drain 5.150 billion pesos from the secondary market on Monday, dealers said.</p>
<p>The Cetes sales were assigned as follows:</p>
<p>    AMOUNT     TERM	 AVERAGE RATE</p>
<p>    150 million    353 days   22.18 pct</p>
<p>    150 million    178 days   21.49 pct</p>
<p>    150 million     87 days   21.41 pct</p>
<p>The terms and maturities of the repurchase agreements were offered as follows:</p>
<p>    500 million     36 days   21.40 pct</p>
<p>    500 million     35 days   21.40 pct</p>
<p>    500 million     30 days   21.48 pct</p>
<p>    550 million     28 days   21.48 pct</p>
<p>    600 million     18 days   21.76 pct</p>
<p>    600 million     16 days   21.70 pct</p>
<p>    600 million     11 days   21.50 pct</p>
<p>    700 million	4 days   20.99 pct</p>
<p>    150 million	1 day    20.07 pct</p>
<p>*Amounts in pesos</p>
<p>(( -- Mexico City newsroom +525 728-9559))</p>
